        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "13c52599-1ad8-58f3-834e-018bd2cf98e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Travis McGee, John D. MacDonald, Janet Evanovich, Stephanie Plum, Rod Taylor, Steffie Hall\n- Works: Travis McGee series, Stephanie Plum series, Darker than Amber\n- Concepts: title theme in detective/mystery fiction, bestseller lists\n\nFacts:\n- John D. MacDonald created Travis McGee as a fictional character.\n- The 21-book Travis McGee series uses color-themed titles and is an early example of a detective or mystery fiction series with a title theme.\n- Janet Evanovich began her career by writing short contemporary romance novels under the pen name Steffie Hall.\n- Janet Evanovich became famous for writing the contemporary mystery series featuring Stephanie Plum, a former lingerie buyer from Trenton, New Jersey, who becomes a bounty hunter after losing her job.\n- The Stephanie Plum novels by Janet Evanovich have appeared on The New York Times, USA Today, The Wall Street Journal, and Amazon bestseller lists.\n- Rod Taylor starred as Travis McGee in the film Darker than Amber.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
